  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656342",
      "title": "Protecting Routes with canActivate",
      "lectureOrder": 471,
      "videoOrder": 432,
      "sourceHash": "5f26acdcbf1571ce1ba9b47be995acf3681dfd323e0cff190d1b1627c58cd12c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 4.59,
          "en": "-: As mentioned in the last lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.59,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "we want to maybe protect some of our routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.41,
          "end": 9.42,
          "en": "And we can use a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 13.17,
          "en": "offered by Angular which allows us to run some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.17,
          "end": 15.81,
          "en": "at a point of time defined by us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.81,
          "end": 18.87,
          "en": "I will add a new file in our route folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.87,
          "end": 22.62,
          "en": "and I will name it auth-guardservice.ts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.62,
          "end": 26.7,
          "en": "because the code we run there is stored in such a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.7,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "I'll name it auth-guard though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "because the feature of the Angular router is called guards.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 35.91,
          "en": "It guards certain actions like navigating to around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 37.113,
          "en": "or away from it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.1,
          "end": 39.837,
          "en": "but in the end it is a normal service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.837,
          "end": 41.4,
          "en": "and therefore as such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.4,
          "end": 44.13,
          "en": "I will export a class which I'll name AuthGuard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.13,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "Now you could add Service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 48.36,
          "en": "to be fully in line with all the other services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.36,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "but since we will only use this as a guard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "I will leave it at the AuthGuard name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 58.73,
          "en": "And now here I will implement the CanActiviate interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "This interface is provided by the Angular router package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 66.09,
          "en": "so you need to import it and it forces you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "to have a CanActivate method in this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "The CanActivate method now will receive two arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 79.377,
          "en": "the ActivatedRouteSnapshot and the state of the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 85.77,
          "en": "so the RouterStateSnapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.77,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "So make sure to also add these imports at the top here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 93.36,
          "en": "from @angularRouter and to add them here as types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.36,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "for the two parameters we get and CanActivate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 99.81,
          "en": "Now you might ask where are we getting these arguments from?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.81,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "Keep in mind we will soon define that Angular should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 105.75,
          "en": "execute this code before a route is loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 108.03,
          "en": "So it will give us this data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 111.47999999999999,
          "en": "and we simply need to be able to handle the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.47999999999999,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "So that is CanActivate with the arguments it requires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 117.99000000000001,
          "en": "CanActivate also returns something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.99000000000001,
          "end": 121.14,
          "en": "It either returns an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.14,
          "end": 126.03,
          "en": "So make sure to import observable from rxjs observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.03,
          "end": 127.893,
          "en": "is the correct path in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 131.97,
          "en": "This observable then will wrap a boolean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.97,
          "end": 135.81,
          "en": "so it will in the end resolve to a true or false value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.81,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "Alternatively, this route returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 142.41,
          "en": "also returning the boolean in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "or it returns just a boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 148.29,
          "en": "So CanActivate can run both asynchronously",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.29,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "returning an observable or a promise or synchronously",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 153.93,
          "en": "because you might have some guards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.93,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "which execute some code which runs completely on the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 159.21,
          "en": "therefore it runs synchronously.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.21,
          "end": 161.37,
          "en": "Or you might have some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.37,
          "end": 163.38,
          "en": "which takes a couple of seconds to finish",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.38,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "because you use a timeout in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 166.53,
          "en": "Or you reach out to a server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.53,
          "end": 168.18,
          "en": "so it runs asynchronously",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.18,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "and both is possible with CanActivate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 172.98,
          "en": "you will see an example in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.98,
          "end": 177.36,
          "en": "So here we want to be able to log in or out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.36,
          "end": 181.65,
          "en": "For this, let's say we have another service the authservice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.73,
          "end": 185.04,
          "en": "and this is just a fake service here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.04,
          "end": 187.86,
          "en": "So I will name it AuthService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.86,
          "end": 191.1,
          "en": "And in a real application this might reach out to a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "and allow us to log in or log out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 196.17000000000002,
          "en": "and check our current authentication state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.17000000000002,
          "end": 199.41,
          "en": "I will track the state here too with the loggedIn property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "which is set to false initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 203.91,
          "en": "And then I'll add a login method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.91,
          "end": 208.17000000000002,
          "en": "which will set loggedIn to true, just like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.17000000000002,
          "end": 212.7,
          "en": "and a logout method which will set loggedIn to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.7,
          "end": 215.37,
          "en": "to again fake this behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.37,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "And I'll have a method which allows us to check the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 221.37,
          "en": "And here I want to simulate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.37,
          "end": 223.17000000000002,
          "en": "that this takes some time to finish",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.17000000000002,
          "end": 225.54,
          "en": "because maybe we reach out to a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.54,
          "end": 229.5,
          "en": "Therefore here I will return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.5,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "a new promise therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 234.72,
          "en": "This promise will as always take a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.72,
          "end": 236.19,
          "en": "a function as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.19,
          "end": 240.99,
          "en": "with the resolve and reject methods we can execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.99,
          "end": 244.83,
          "en": "And in this promise, here I will execute set time out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.83,
          "end": 247.65,
          "en": "to wait let's say 800 milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.65,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "and then execute another method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 252.24,
          "en": "in which I will resolve the promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.24,
          "end": 253.89,
          "en": "and return this loggedIn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.89,
          "end": 256.74,
          "en": "Again, just to fake that, this takes a couple of seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.74,
          "end": 259.41,
          "en": "to finish or sometime to finish.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.41,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "So with this AuthService added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.32,
          "en": "I now want to use it in my AuthGuard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 265.32,
          "end": 267.69,
          "en": "And as this is all just a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 267.69,
          "end": 270.81,
          "en": "we need to add @Injectable to be able to reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.81,
          "end": 274.5,
          "en": "to the other service to injected service into this guard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.5,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "So make sure to import, @injectable from Angular core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 281.7,
          "en": "and then I will add a constructor to my AuthGuard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.7,
          "end": 285.09000000000003,
          "en": "where I reach out to my fake AuthService here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 286.47,
          "en": "of type Angular service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 286.47,
          "end": 289.83,
          "en": "Therefore make sure to add this import too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 289.83,
          "end": 292.71,
          "en": "And now in the CanActivate guard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 292.71,
          "end": 296.373,
          "en": "I simply want to check whether the user is logged in or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 300.642,
          "en": "So here I can reach out to my AuthService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.642,
          "end": 302.22,
          "en": "to the isAuthenticate method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.22,
          "end": 306.36,
          "en": "which again keep in mind returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 306.36,
          "end": 309.36,
          "en": "while therefore we should return this promise here I guess.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 309.36,
          "end": 311.103,
          "en": "So it returns us this promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 311.97,
          "end": 314.85,
          "en": "And here I then want to be able to handle that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 314.85,
          "end": 318.183,
          "en": "whenever this promise and the AuthService resolves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 319.14,
          "end": 324.14,
          "en": "I know that there I will get back a boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 324.33,
          "end": 328.44,
          "en": "So this authentication state, this loggedIn boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 328.44,
          "end": 330.75,
          "en": "it is what we resolve here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 330.75,
          "end": 332.67,
          "en": "And this could be false or true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.67,
          "end": 335.37,
          "en": "So I know that I will get back a boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 335.37,
          "end": 338.82,
          "en": "And here I then want to check if this is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 338.82,
          "end": 340.93,
          "en": "in which case I want to return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 341.94,
          "end": 345.42,
          "en": "and otherwise I want to navigate away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 345.42,
          "end": 347.52,
          "en": "because I don't want to allow the user access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 347.52,
          "end": 350.37,
          "en": "to the route he wanted to go to originally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 350.37,
          "end": 352.68,
          "en": "I will navigate a way to force the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 352.68,
          "end": 354.69,
          "en": "to go somewhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 354.69,
          "end": 357.24,
          "en": "So I will inject the Angular router for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 357.24,
          "end": 359.04,
          "en": "because this is how we can navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 359.04,
          "end": 360.48,
          "en": "with the navigate method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 360.48,
          "end": 364.62,
          "en": "Make sure to add the import from @angular router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 364.62,
          "end": 368.04,
          "en": "and then here we can navigate with the navigate method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 368.04,
          "end": 370.62,
          "en": "Let's say we just want to go back to our route page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 370.62,
          "end": 372.36,
          "en": "with just slash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 372.36,
          "end": 376.98,
          "en": "So in this case our CanActivate method will navigate away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 376.98,
          "end": 379.35,
          "en": "and it will now simply return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 379.35,
          "end": 382.53,
          "en": "this promise it still is in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 382.53,
          "end": 384.69,
          "en": "because if we return something inside of the promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.69,
          "end": 387.27,
          "en": "it will give us back another promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.27,
          "end": 389.52,
          "en": "So now we're returning a promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 389.52,
          "end": 392.97,
          "en": "which gives us back true or simply navigates us away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 392.97,
          "end": 396.03,
          "en": "canceling the old navigation anyways therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 396.03,
          "end": 399.69,
          "en": "So this now allows us to control access to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
